      "id": "bootstrap-initialise",
      "name": "BootstrapInitialise",
      "category": "LowLevelMemTracker",
      "signature": "BootstrapInitialise(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FLowLevelMemTracker*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Initialize the data required for tracking allocations if it has not already been done.\nThis can occur after construction of the singleton FLowLevelMemTracker.\nThis function is called automatically by any LLM function that requires it, but can also be triggered\nby external systems that need to carefully manage static initialization order.\nBootstrapInitialize does NOT make GetTagUniqueName available; that requires FinishInitialize."
    },
    {
      "id": "finish-initialise",
      "name": "FinishInitialise",
      "category": "LowLevelMemTracker",
      "signature": "FinishInitialise(Target)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FLowLevelMemTracker*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "Finish initialization if not already done. Calls BootstrapInitialise if necessary. After being called,\nall functions in LLM including those returning FNames are available.\nThis function should be called as soon as possible after FNames are available so that other tracking\nsystems reliant on LLM's FName data can start tracking as soon as possible."
    },
